# "Whenever this creature deals combat damage to a player, you may sacrifice it. If you do, proliferate." With the trigger
# on the stack, Bot2 takes the Scamp with Old Man of the Sea (power 1 is no more than Old Man's 2; Bot2 has controlled
# Old Man since their turn began, CR 302.6). As the trigger resolves, its controller, Bot1, can't sacrifice a permanent
# they don't control (CR 701.21a), so the sacrifice is an impossible option and isn't offered (CR 608.2d): Bot1 isn't
# asked, nothing is sacrificed (Bot1's graveyard stays empty, the Scamp stays Bot2's, no dies trigger hits anyone) and
# nothing proliferates (Bot2's Liliana of the Veil keeps 3 loyalty).

[Bot1 Deck]
Cacophony Scamp
Mountain x7
Mountain x16

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Island
Old Man of the Sea
Swamp
Liliana of the Veil
Island x20

[Actions]
